---
// Mars's lite route — where a visitor goes who cannot, or will not, run the Mars globe.
//
// TEMPORARY BY DESIGN, AND THE REGISTRY IS WHAT MAKES IT CHEAP TO REPLACE. `BODIES.mars.liteRoute`
// names this path; the pre-paint guard and the view bar's tier picker both read it from there, so
// rewriting this page, or moving it, is this file plus one string. Nothing links here by hand.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS AT ALL, given Earth's lite route is the gallery. The tier ladder always has a
// destination: a device with no WebGL2 is redirected off a globe before the page paints, and a
// visitor can pick Lite in the view bar on purpose. Sending either of them to `/` would answer "this
// device cannot draw Mars" by showing them Earth. What it cannot do is show hero renders instead,
// because Mars has none — so it says so rather than pretending the gap is a design.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Masthead from "../../components/Masthead.astro";
import { bodyRoutes } from "../../lib/bodyRoutes";

const routes = bodyRoutes("mars");
---

<Base
  title="Mars — Terrella"
  description="Mars without the globe, for devices that cannot draw one."
  body="mars"
  quality={true}
>
  <Masthead
    heading="Mars"
    eyebrow="Without the globe"
    legend={false}
    back="/"
    backLabel="← Gallery"
    maxWidth="min(1500px, 92vw)"
  />

  <main class="lite">
    <p class="lede">This device is seeing Mars without the globe.</p>
    <p>
      The globe is a WebGL2 map of shaded relief, and you are here because either your browser
      cannot run one or you chose Lite in the view controls. On Earth that choice lands you in a
      gallery of ray-traced renders; Mars has no renders yet, so there is nothing to put here in
      their place.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both of those are open questions rather than oversights — a Mars look has not been decided,
      and the renders come after it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="onward" href={routes.globe}>Go to Mars →</a>
      <a class="onward" href="/earth/">Go to the Earth globe →</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .lite {
    max-width: min(1500px, 92vw);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 clamp(1.1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) 5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .lite p {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    /* The one place the body's accent appears on this page, which makes a provisional colour
       visible to anyone judging it. */
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 0.75rem;
  }
  .onward {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-right: 1.5rem;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .onward:hover,
  .onward:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
